---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../utils/content.js";

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Privacy Policy", href: "/privacy-policy/" }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | LeashFree.ca"
  description="Read how LeashFree.ca collects, uses, and protects information across dog park guides, local directories, maps, calculators, comparison tools, ads, and sponsored links."
  canonical="https://leashfree.ca/privacy-policy/"
  structuredData={breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs)}
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="summary">
        How LeashFree.ca handles information when you browse our guides, use our tools, view maps, or interact with links and ads.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section>
    <div class="legal-content">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> May 31, 2026</p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>LeashFree.ca</strong> collects, uses, and protects information when you
        use our website. LeashFree.ca provides dog park guides, dog breed content, local pet business directories,
        maps, calculators, comparison tools, articles, sponsored content, and other resources for Canadian dog owners.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect the following types of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage and device information:</strong> Browser type, device type, operating system, pages viewed,
          referring pages, approximate location inferred from IP address, time spent on pages, and similar analytics
          data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you provide:</strong> Details you choose to send us, such as feedback, correction
          requests, suggested listings, names, email addresses, messages, or other content submitted through contact or
          submission features.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tool inputs:</strong> Information entered into calculators, comparison tools, search fields, filters,
          quizzes, or finder tools, such as dog weight, activity level, food selections, location searches, or naming
          preferences. We use these inputs to provide the requested result and improve site functionality.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Location information:</strong> If you use a "Use my location" map feature, your browser may ask for
          permission to share your device location. We use that location in your browser to sort or filter nearby
          results. You can deny or revoke location permission through your browser settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We use information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate, maintain, and improve LeashFree.ca</li>
        <li>Provide search, map, calculator, comparison, and finder features</li>
        <li>Respond to messages, correction requests, listing suggestions, or feedback</li>
        <li>Review content quality, usage trends, errors, and site performance</li>
        <li>Protect the website from spam, misuse, scraping, fraud, or security issues</li>
        <li>Display, measure, and improve advertising, sponsorship, and affiliate-related content</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We and third-party providers may use cookies, pixels, local browser storage, or similar technologies to operate
        site features, understand traffic, remember basic preferences, measure ads, and support advertising. You can
        control cookies through your browser settings. Some features may not work as expected if cookies or browser
        storage are disabled.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Analytics, Ads, Maps, and Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>LeashFree.ca may use third-party services, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics services</strong> to understand site traffic and improve content</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense and advertising partners</strong> to display and measure ads</li>
        <li><strong>Map providers</strong>, including OpenStreetMap, Leaflet, and Google Maps links or embeds</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting, security, development, and content infrastructure providers</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate, sponsor, or retailer links</strong> that may identify LeashFree.ca as a referral source</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These third parties may collect information under their own privacy policies. We do not control their practices.
        To learn more about how Google uses information from partner sites, visit
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Google's Privacy and Terms
        </a>. You can adjust personalized ad settings through
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Sponsored, Affiliate, and External Links</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages may include sponsored placements, product links, retailer links, affiliate links, or links to dog
        food brands, pet businesses, municipalities, rescue groups, veterinarians, trainers, stores, or other external
        websites. If you click an external link, the destination site may collect information about your visit. Their
        privacy policies apply once you leave LeashFree.ca.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We may share limited information with
        service providers who help us operate the site, analyze traffic, secure the site, deliver ads, or manage
        sponsored and affiliate programs. We may also disclose information if required by law or if needed to protect
        our website, users, rights, or property.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Retention and Security</h2>
      <p>
        We keep information only as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described in this policy, unless a longer
        period is required or permitted by law. We use reasonable safeguards, but no website, network, or transmission
        method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your Choices</h2>
      <p>You can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Disable or delete cookies through your browser settings</li>
        <li>Deny or revoke browser location permissions</li>
        <li>Opt out of personalized advertising through participating ad platforms</li>
        <li>Contact us to request access, correction, or deletion of personal information you provided</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        LeashFree.ca is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>10. External Links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website links to third-party websites and services. We are not responsible for their content, accuracy,
        security, or privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised
        "Last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us through the contact options
        available on LeashFree.ca.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-content {
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal-content p,
  .legal-content li {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
</style>
